# Conversational search (DR-11). Three layers, in order of authority:
#
#   1. CHAT_MVP_ENABLED           master switch. Read at SERVER START via
#                                 publicRuntimeConfig ⇒ changing it is a pod
#                                 restart, not a rebuild. ⚠️ Deliberately NOT named
#                                 NEXT_PUBLIC_*: the Dockerfile runs `npm run build`
#                                 with no build args, so a NEXT_PUBLIC_* read from
#                                 client code inlines as `undefined` in the
#                                 production image — the flag could never turn on
#                                 and there would be no seconds-level kill-switch.
#   2. GrowthBook `conversational_search`   the ROLLOUT control: instant on/off,
#                                 percentage, sticky on terminal_id.
#   3. ?chatPreview=<KEY>         see it on production while the rollout is at 0%.
#                                 Bypasses the percentage ONLY.
#
# Three further gates are code, not env (src/modules/chat/chatEligibility.ts),
# because they must not be switchable by mistake:
#   - own-host allow-list  ⇒ never on nobat.*.ac.ir or any partner/white-label host
#   - empty partnerKey     ⇒ second layer for a partner served from our own host
#   - logged-in only       ⇒ the agreed shape of the initial rollout
CHAT_MVP_ENABLED=false
CHAT_MVP_PREVIEW_KEY=
CHAT_API_BASE=https://j-n-khesht.yazd.p24cloud.ir
